moe/shizuku/api/BinderContainer.java. Original wire names are required for IPC.

Gradle launcher scripts and wrapper JAR were obtained from Nightzuku revision
ca02387ec272f5bf57b0cb3ccf80b3a5bffab944. Gradle wrapper: Copyright Gradle contributors,
Apache-2.0, https://github.com/gradle/gradle. No Nightzuku artwork is included.

Architecture references (no wholesale code import): Porter by darken and
contributors; Nightzuku by kerneldroid and contributors; Shevery by HmnDev-Tech
and contributors; AxManager by fahrez182 and contributors. See docs/UPSTREAMS.md.

Shevery 14.6.5 (HmnDev-Tech/shevery f1f45543e16f98ae4c729721226893c32be130a5,
Apache-2.0) is the reference for the Shevery module ZIP/WebUI contract, lifecycle
automation, diagnostics, device protection and Device Owner controls. The
implementations in Kizuku use its own host, consent and authorization paths.

Runtime/build dependencies retain their own licenses, including AndroidX
(Apache-2.0), Kotlin (Apache-2.0), Rikka Hidden API and Refine (Apache-2.0), and Shizuku SDK
(Apache-2.0; test-client only). JUnit (EPL-1.0) is test-only.
A component-level notice pass is required before any new vendored dependency.

ADB key storage, pairing client and JNI SPAKE2/AEAD adapter are adapted from
d4rken-org/porter revision a288febb4e42b7acb6544cc1b50c89899a22ec4d
(Apache-2.0), originating in stock Shizuku. Adaptations: Kizuku namespace, public
TLS exporter on API31+, bounded local-device transport, code/key log removal,
correct DEVICE_GUID type, explicit cancellation, fail-closed key persistence.
Native BoringSSL prefab 20251124: see BORINGSSL-LICENSE.txt. Bouncy Castle 1.86:
see BOUNCYCASTLE-LICENSE.txt. These licenses are bundled with the application.

The legacy UserService launch/classloading and rish wire follow RikkaApps/Shizuku
b844bc491f1790c72328e1a8e5b2349f8978f0ea and Shizuku-API
a27f6e4151ba7b39965ca47edb2bf0aeed7102e5 (Apache-2.0). Kizuku supplies
its own caller authorization, subprocess lifecycle, and rish JNI bridge.

The Axeron v3 wire includes five unmodified frb.axeron.server AIDL files
and Java parcelable equivalents of the matching upstream Kotlin payloads.
Source: fahrez182/Axeron-API bfceee9cecfb0451448b3453017b8326ee1f591e, MIT.
See AXERON-API-LICENSE.txt. The wire's RikkaX ParcelableList 2.0.1
dependency is MIT. No AxManager BusyBox, resetprop, or artwork is included.

The rish export includes the unmodified Shizuku v13.6.0 launcher and loader
DEX (RikkaApps/Shizuku revision 2650830c5b099ae0dd34fedf614d4f592ca05d65).
The export bundles the Apache-2.0 license and source notice.

Terminal rendering and emulation includes Termux terminal-emulator and terminal-view
Java/resources, revision 8629e632fcb95da272221be327db653fb24befe9,
https://github.com/termux/termux-app. Copyright Termux contributors and the
Android Terminal Emulator authors. These modules are Apache-2.0 exceptions
under Termux's LICENSE.md. See TERMINAL-LICENSE.txt.
Kizuku replaces TerminalSession with its Binder transport adapter and excludes
the Termux app, JNI process launcher, and native libraries.

Native axsh stream framing follows Axeron-API revision
37eb6a3521828458394797e7166ff2e90946304e, MIT, Copyright (c) 2025-2026 FahrezRB.
Kizuku implements that wire in its single host with verified peer credentials,
per-client capability checks, limits and process cleanup.

The bundled js/kernelsu.js and js/axeron.js WebUI helpers are unchanged AxManager source,
revision 7ed7f508464076d2617a9172c9de5bca2e7bcf7a, Apache-2.0.
Kizuku's WebUI bridge supplies its own authorization, origin isolation,
streaming processes, package metadata and lifecycle cleanup.
